The following are the inteinsics that you pickup up when eating corpses...
a human (includes SHK, nurses, and were-things in human form):
	aggravate monster
a cat or dog: aggravate monster
a cockatrive or medusa (haha): turn to stone
a lizard: reverse stoning process, cure stunned and confused effects
a were-thing: become werething
a wraith: gain level
a nurse: heal fully
a invis. stalker: invisiblity (temp) and see invis
a yellow light, giant bat or bat: stunned for a bit
a mimic: imitate a pile o gold for a while
a floating eye: telepathy
a quantum mechanic: change speed
a chameleon: poly self
a voilet fungus: hallucinatation

otherwise, there is a~ 15% chance of getting an intinsic that the monster
may have, for example, eating a red fungus can give you fire resisatnce
 (only 10% for teleportation)

actually, the formula for intrisic determination is that you get it if
the monster level exceeds a random number up to 15.

One question: where did the dev team decide that a lizard corpse is that
powerful?  The only place that I can think of is the Dragonlance 1st series,
1st book, where Raistlin befriend Bupu, who uses the lizard corpse to 'cure'
sicknesses and stuff.


